<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        OSS Release (this file): Developer ID signed, NOT sandboxed.

        Why not sandboxed: Sparkle's installer needs to replace the app
        bundle on disk. Doing that inside an App Sandbox requires shipping
        Sparkle's XPC installer + downloader services as embedded targets
        plus a non-trivial set of temporary-exception mach-lookup
        entitlements. We opt out of that complexity here — Developer ID +
        notarization is what Gatekeeper expects for non-MAS distribution,
        and a non-sandboxed Developer-ID app is perfectly acceptable
        outside the Mac App Store.

        A separate MDPrintView-mas.entitlements (with sandbox + Sparkle
        XPC services, OR without Sparkle entirely since MAS handles
        updates) will be added when the Mac App Store SKU ships.

        Hardened Runtime is still enabled in the build settings (required
        for notarization) — that's separate from sandboxing.
    -->

    <!-- Explicitly DENY debugger attach. If this file has no entitlements
         declared at all, Xcode falls back to a default that sets
         get-task-allow=true. Notarization rejects any app where
         get-task-allow is true, so we set it false here unconditionally. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
